<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office during the Friday to Sunday weekend, according to studio estimates released by Exhibitor Relations Co. Final data will be released on Monday.</p>
<p>(Last weekend's position in parenthesis, * = new release).</p>
<p>    1 (1) First Wives Club ................. $15.5 million</p>
<p>    2 (*) Extreme Measures .................  $7.1 million</p>
<p>    3 (2) Last Man Standing ................. $4.1 million</p>
<p>    4 (*) 2 Days in the Valley .............. $3.5 million</p>
<p>    5 (3) Fly Away Home ..................... $3.2 million</p>
<p>    6 (9) Independence Day .................. $2.5 million</p>
<p>    7=(5) Bulletproof ....................... $1.9 million</p>
<p>    7=(6) First Kid ......................... $1.9 million</p>
<p>    9 (4) Maximum Risk ...................... $1.7 million</p>
<p>    10(7) Tin Cup ........................... $1.2 million</p>
<p>NOTE: First Wives Club is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.. &quot;Extreme Measures&quot;, &quot;Fly Away Home&quot; and &quot;Maximum Risk&quot; are released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.. &quot;Last Man Standing&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Turner Broadcasting System Inc. 2 Days in the Valley is released by MGM, which is being bought by a consortium backed by investor Kirk Kerkorian. &quot;Independence Day&quot; is released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox. &quot;Bulletproof&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.. &quot;First Kid&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co.. &quot;Tin Cup&quot; is released by Time Warner Inc.'s Warner Bros.</p>
